<section id="next" aria-labelledby="next-title" class="y57">
<div class="y58">
<p class="y59">Coming in 0.6.</p>
<div class="y60">
<div class="y61">
<h2 id="next-title" class="y62">What 0.6 is built around.</h2>
<p class="y63">In development. Follow the work on <a href="https://github.com/izyuumi/yorozu" class="y16">GitHub</a>.</p>
</div>
<div class="y64">
<div class="y65">
<h3 class="y66">One conversation that stays</h3>
<p class="y67">You keep a single thread with your secretary instead of opening a new one for every task. It carries on from where you left off.</p>
</div>
<div class="y65">
<h3 class="y66">Workers, in layers</h3>
<p class="y67">The secretary hands work to workers. A worker can pass part of its job to workers of its own, and each one reports back up the chain.</p>
</div>
<div class="y65">
<h3 class="y66">PAIOS memory</h3>
<p class="y67">One memory layer for knowledge, history and retrieval: what you have told it, what has happened, and how it finds both again.</p>
</div>
<div class="y65">
<h3 class="y66">A private runtime on your Mac</h3>
<p class="y67">The secretary and its workers are planned to run on your own Mac, the machine you already host Yorozu on.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</section>

<section id="today" aria-labelledby="today-title" class="y68">
<div class="y69">
<div class="y70">
<div class="y71">
<div class="y61">
<h2 id="today-title" class="y72">Use Yorozu 0.5 today.</h2>
<p class="y73">Your Mac hosts the agents through OpenClaw. Your iPhone reaches them: start a task on the train, answer a permission request from the lock screen, read the result at your desk.</p>
</div>
<dl class="y74">
<div class="y54">
<dt class="y75">Approve from your phone</dt>
<dd class="y76">When an agent wants to run a command, send a message or spend money, the question arrives as a card you can allow, refuse or discuss first.</dd>
</div>
<div class="y54">
<dt class="y75">Threads on every device</dt>
<dd class="y76">Threads sync between the Mac and every paired device, iPhone Duo included. Pair several Macs and see them in one list.</dd>
</div>
<div class="y54">
<dt class="y75">Search and share</dt>
<dd class="y76">Search the full history on your Mac, and send a link, some text or a photo into a thread from the share sheet.</dd>
</div>
<div class="y54">
<dt class="y75">Encrypted end to end</dt>
<dd class="y76">Messages are encrypted between your iPhone and your Mac. The relay in the middle sees size and timing. No Yorozu account is needed.</dd>
</div>
</dl>
</div>

